766
01:11:59,406 --> 01:12:07,140
so one thing that we talked about a little bit earlier was a handful of things that single agents struggle with.

767
01:12:07,776 --> 01:12:14,896
And this is a big takeaway that we learned as part of dynamic workflows, and I wanted to just talk a little bit about them and how they apply to uh

768
01:12:15,056 --> 01:12:18,084
sort of from from Cloud Code and how they apply to cloud managed agents.

769
01:12:18,574 --> 01:12:23,268
So one is agentic laziness, another is self-preferential bias, and the third is goal drift.

770
01:12:24,686 --> 01:12:34,788
So um it turns out that like if our prompt is something like we are having an outage right now, please go look at these 50 different services

