01:12:44,878 --> 01:12:46,180
Go research, is there an outage?

773
01:12:46,574 --> 01:12:47,460
Don't touch production.

774
01:12:48,174 --> 01:12:58,416
A single agent might have this problem where after it sees 35 services are healthy, then it starts to like convince itself that, oh, it's like everything looks good, it's probably fine.

775
01:12:58,496 --> 01:13:01,668
Like I don't really actually need to look at the rest of the services.

776
01:13:01,856 --> 01:13:07,856
So we have seen that agentic laziness can be like one of the things that a single agent will run into.

777
01:13:08,046 --> 01:13:11,716
And after it's seen so many that are good, it can kind of just be like, okay, I think we're good.

778
01:13:11,982 --> 01:13:17,380
Let me just not look at the rest and let's save some tokens and tell our human that we're good to go.

779
01:13:18,350 --> 01:13:27,376
Coordinator runs into a sort of a similar problem where you might have three subagents reporting back to the reporter or to the coordinator, and the coordinator still has to

